> is it really depends on the actual code you're using. What you shared is really not saying anything at all, because it's unclear what objects you're assigning and what are the evaluations. It's really up to you application to decide what re-oreding and consolidation is possible - it has really nothing to do with Rserve. Rserve itself supports assignments of complex objects, so it's entirely up to the application to decide what to push when. Just like in any R session make sure you're removing objects you don't need etc. Without actual code or an idea of what you are trying to push it's really impossible to asses anything. Conceptually, Rserve is only facilitating the serialization in and out, everything else is up to the R code you're using - nothing to do with Rserve itself... If you can provide more, we can try to help.
